 11    22      2     1                     1         4                 5
 13    26      2     0                     2         4                 1
   NOTE: g(2p)-g(p) = 0,0,1,1,2 (p=3,5,7,11,13) = the NEWFORM count at level 2p = the residual dim.
        (n=14: 1 newform = f_14 = curve 14a; the genus JUMP is the newform, S56-58.)

================================================================================================
(III) THE rho<->R LEVER, honest degrees: THM-580 (u=2t) = degree 2; degeneracy = degree 3
================================================================================================
   p=7, n=14: THM-580 circle descent DEGREE=2 (u=2t); modular degeneracy DEGREE=3 (Gamma_0(2) index)
   p=11, n=22: THM-580 circle descent DEGREE=2 (u=2t); modular degeneracy DEGREE=3 (Gamma_0(2) index)
   p=13, n=26: THM-580 circle descent DEGREE=2 (u=2t); modular degeneracy DEGREE=3 (Gamma_0(2) index)
   => S58's 'peel = degree-3 degeneracy' is a SHAPE match, not a degree match. The degree-2
      candidate is Atkin-Lehner W_2 (an involution). Compute W_2 fixed points (class numbers):
   X_0(6): g=0; if g(X_0(6)/W_2)=0 then W_2 has f=2+2*0-0=2 fixed points (RH deg 2)
   X_0(10): g=0; if g(X_0(10)/W_2)=0 then W_2 has f=2+2*0-0=2 fixed points (RH deg 2)
   X_0(14): g=1; if g(X_0(14)/W_2)=0 then W_2 has f=2+2*1-0=4 fixed points (RH deg 2)
   X_0(22): g=2; if g(X_0(22)/W_2)=0 then W_2 has f=2+2*2-0=6 fixed points (RH deg 2)
   X_0(26): g=2; if g(X_0(26)/W_2)=0 then W_2 has f=2+2*2-0=6 fixed points (RH deg 2)

================================================================================================
(IV) NICHE: Phi_6(n) factorization, Dedekind sum, and a covering-min hunt
================================================================================================
   n  Phi6=n^2-n+1           factor    s(n,Phi6)  covmin n/Phi6
   6            31               31        -5/62           6/31
  10            91             7*13      -15/182          10/91
  14           183             3*61     -91/1098         14/183
  22           463              463      -77/926         22/463
  26           651           3*7*31    -325/3906         26/651
   8            57             3*19      -14/171           8/57
  12           133             7*19      -11/133         12/133
   Phi6(14)=183=3*61 (large prime 61); Phi6(26)=651=3*7*31. The large prime factor of Phi6
   is the covering-min binding's arithmetic core (HYP-3732 Farey rung).
